{
  "id": "holey_songhay_zarma",
  "name": "Holey (Songhay-Zarma spirit-possession music)",
  "family": "global",
  "lineage": "Music of the holey spirit-possession ceremonies of the Songhay and Zarma of western Niger and the Gao region of Mali, in which mediums are possessed by spirits, among them the hauka, each family called by its own melodies and praise mottoes. The godji, a one-string bowed fiddle, carries the spirit melodies over gourd drums beaten with sticks, while sorko praise-singers address the spirits. Bernard Surugue documented its music and Jean Rouch filmed its ceremonies. The goje card stands in for the godji and the inverted-calabash card for the gourd drums.",
  "recipe": "classic modern holey, ritual Devotional, indigenous branch. solo with instrumental accompaniment, single lead single track no stacking. ostinato trance goje, gourd mid strong calabash inverted calabash. field recording. ORTF stereo pair, portable field-recorder pre. 24-bit digital.",
